# Copy this file to .env for local development. Never commit .env.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flask + Routes: you do not need any of this. The app runs with no .env at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# FLASK_SECRET_KEY signs session cookies. Without it the app still starts, but
# makes up a throwaway key each time, so anyone logged in gets logged out on
# every restart. Set it once you have logins.
# Generate one with:  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
FLASK_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database + SQL onward: your database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your database already exists - it was created together with your app and
# carries the same name, with dashes turned into underscores. Everything you
# need is on the Deployments page in the course sidebar, or run:
#
#   ssh dokku@iscs2.gcsu.edu mysql:url yournetid-6200
#
# Leave this empty and the app runs fine without a database - the Examples page
# just explains that there is not one yet.
#
# The host is 172.17.0.1, NOT localhost: your app runs in a container, and
# inside it localhost means the container. That also means this same line will
# not connect from your laptop. Keep it anyway, and test data pages on the live
# site.
#
#   mysql://username:password@host:3306/database_name
#
# If your password contains @ / # or +, percent-encode it (@ becomes %40).
DATABASE_URL=
